@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Tournament help";
}
<section class="form-page help-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Tournament-day guide</p>
    <h1>Run a local tournament with confidence</h1>
    <p class="lede">Pocket Rankings keeps registration, the draw, table calls, scores, corrections, and retained results in one event record.</p>

    <div class="help-grid">
        <article class="panel"><span>1</span><h2>Create the event</h2><p>Enter the venue and local start time. New events remain private drafts until an authorized organizer opens registration.</p></article>
        <article class="panel"><span>2</span><h2>Build competitions</h2><p>Choose single elimination, double elimination, or round robin; set the game, entrant type, races, handicap use, and player-facing rules.</p></article>
        <article class="panel"><span>3</span><h2>Register and check in</h2><p>Add local entrant names without requiring an account. Waitlisted, withdrawn, and disqualified records remain retained but do not enter the draw.</p></article>
        <article class="panel"><span>4</span><h2>Publish the draw</h2><p>Verify the field, choose seeded, randomized, or manual ordering, and publish an immutable draw revision. Registration then locks.</p></article>
        <article class="panel"><span>5</span><h2>Run the floor</h2><p>Add venue tables, assign a ready match, call it, start it, and record the confirmed result. A table cannot host two active matches.</p></article>
        <article class="panel"><span>6</span><h2>Correct safely</h2><p>Score corrections retain their versions. If the winner changes, an Owner or Tournament Director must explicitly reset every affected later match.</p></article>
        <article class="panel"><span>7</span><h2>Share the live display</h2><p>After registration opens, activate a temporary Live Tournament Link. Copy it or print its QR code immediately; it expires automatically and archival ends it.</p></article>
        <article class="panel"><span>8</span><h2>Complete and retain</h2><p>Finish every required match, complete each competition, then complete and archive the event. Permanent results and organizer history remain readable.</p></article>
        <article class="panel"><span>9</span><h2>Print and export</h2><p>Use Print on a public event for brackets or schedules. Authorized directors can export entrants, results, standings, and audit history as safe CSV files.</p></article>
    </div>

    <section class="panel page-section"><h2>Role boundaries</h2><p><strong>Owners</strong> manage all Tournament events and access. <strong>Tournament Directors</strong> manage only assigned events. <strong>Scorekeepers</strong> can view assigned events and operate only assigned matches.</p><p>Production organizer access stays closed unless the separate Account service confirms identity and a current Tournament entitlement.</p></section>
</section>
